Kontrol-ID provides a managed Squid and E2Guardian traffic chain for transparent
Windows user identification or explicit Kerberos/SPNEGO, legacy NTLM and Basic
proxy authentication. It includes a compiled external ACL helper, secure
endpoint enrollment, an assisted AD/keytab workflow, a fallback login portal,
ICAP identity forwarding, and XMLRPC configuration synchronization.

The helper communicates directly with enrolled Windows hosts over WinRM HTTPS.
No persistent Kontrol service is installed on Windows endpoints. Kerberos is
the recommended explicit authentication method; NTLM is opt-in compatibility.
